1
00:00:27,555 --> 00:00:35,288
Warm room, hot tea.
Hands on the keys.

2
00:00:39,022 --> 00:00:47,333
He lifts his hands high.
Music fills the sky.

3
00:00:50,755 --> 00:00:58,666
“Play it soft, play it loud.”
He guides me, soft and proud.

4
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:09,288
We talk of life and death.
Music is my breath.

5
00:01:12,977 --> 00:01:21,955
He asks how I feel.
I hide what’s too real.

6
00:01:24,111 --> 00:01:32,288
Lioness under my skin.
Sleeping where dark begins.

7
00:01:34,977 --> 00:01:43,422
Quiet pain, buried deep.
Secrets I will keep.

8
00:01:46,455 --> 00:01:54,633
Words she left unsaid.
Tears I never shed.

9
00:01:56,855 --> 00:02:05,566
I can’t leave the safe and small.
They caught me when I hit the wall.

10
00:02:08,655 --> 00:02:19,189
Walking away feels like a crime.
But the big beast needs my time.

11
00:02:21,822 --> 00:02:31,333
Loyalty fights the old ghost.
The quiet words that hurt the most

12
00:02:32,589 --> 00:02:44,589
Torn between the kids I love,
And the roaring sky above.

13
00:03:04,877 --> 00:03:13,633
The tea grows cold and still.
His voice gives me a thrill.

14
00:03:15,756 --> 00:03:23,312
He leans across the wood.
A promise understood.

15
00:03:26,512 --> 00:03:34,156
“Come with me.
To a house of light.

16
00:03:37,268 --> 00:03:45,490
A big choir waits.
Behind the heavy gates.”

17
00:03:47,401 --> 00:03:56,912
“An old pipe organ stands.
Wood and metal, strong and grand.

18
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:07,490
Nineteen-thirty-six, the year.
A mighty beast to steer.

19
00:04:09,471 --> 00:04:18,094
We must shake the stone.
Before the world turns bone.

20
00:04:19,844 --> 00:04:28,999
Keep the freezing night away.
Make the heavens sway.”

21
00:04:30,955 --> 00:04:40,244
I can’t leave the safe and small.
They caught me when I hit the wall.

22
00:04:41,222 --> 00:04:53,488
Walking away feels like a crime.
But the big beast needs my time.

23
00:04:55,577 --> 00:05:04,377
Loyalty fights the old ghost.
The quiet words that hurt the most.

24
00:05:06,688 --> 00:05:15,399
Torn between the kids I love,
And the roaring sky above.

